Z||000000||Alex4mula||07-10-2001||09:57 PM||||The driver side PM in my new car (Formula) is not moving but you can hear the motor turning. I looked inside and found out that the two little screws that push & pull are missing. Are those easy to find or buy? Easy to reinstall? Is this fixable or do I need to replace the whole mirror assembly?<P>TIA <BR><P>------------------<BR>Alex4mula<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.zing.com/picture/p69fbfe3e99ec5a0b81c10afcc578ff95/fe6d5c42.jpg.orig.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000001||sombre||07-10-2001||11:21 PM||||  Don't know if you can buy them by themselves or not.I got a replacement for one I lost at the local pick & pull...'80's F-bodies used the same mirror assy and are much easier to find.<BR> <BR>                             Greg<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000002||GT-maniac||07-11-2001||12:56 AM||||Look for late 80's era firebirds in your local wreckers. May be hard to find though an amazing number of birds were sold with manual mirrors. Once you find one with power mirrors carefully pry out the center of the mirror assembly. What your trying to do is pry out the cross shaped piece that holds the mirror into the motor housing. If you can get that out you can just pull the mirror off. The movement rods will pull out of the housing easily. Then just snap the rods into the back of the mirror casing and push the cross shaped thing back into motor housing in your mirror housing. Take care to ensure that you've got the posts lined up with the right holes. It's fairly easy to do the only tricky part is getting that cross to snap back into its mounts on the motor housing. <p>[This message has been edited by GT-maniac (edited 07-11-2001).]||||reg||1
